From: Koral Ilgun <koral.ilgun@adtran.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: skip a BSS entry with probe data of an old channel

After a channel switch, cfg80211_update_assoc_bss_entry() moves the
entry of the current BSS to the new channel. Unless an entry of the
new channel replaces it, the entry keeps the probe response data of
the old channel, and cfg80211_update_known_bss() lets only a probe
response replace them, not a beacon.

mac80211 takes the operating parameters of the next association from
these data. With the HT Operation element of the old channel,
ieee80211_determine_ap_chan() sees a wrong control channel, and the
station connects without HT, VHT, HE and EHT. For a visible SSID the
beacons keep the entry current, so this has no time limit.

Mark the moved entry, and do not return a marked entry that nothing
holds from __cfg80211_get_bss(), as for an expired one. A new
connection then gets ENOENT, and wpa_supplicant scans the channel for
the BSS before it tries again. A probe response clears the mark. The
data stay in the entry, because the entry of a hidden SSID needs them
for its SSID and no beacon can replace them. A held entry is still
returned, so a new authentication from the connected state keeps the
old data.

Fixes: 0afd425b1b64 ("cfg80211: fix duplicated scan entries after channel switch")
---
 net/wireless/core.h |    5 +++++
 net/wireless/scan.c |   17 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

--- a/net/wireless/core.h
+++ b/net/wireless/core.h
@@ -213,6 +213,11 @@ struct cfg80211_internal_bss {
 
 	enum bss_source_type bss_source;
 
+	/* the probe response data are from the channel before a channel
+	 * switch moved this entry; beacons do not replace them
+	 */
+	bool proberesp_stale;
+
 	/* must be last because of priv member */
 	struct cfg80211_bss pub;
 };
--- a/net/wireless/scan.c
+++ b/net/wireless/scan.c
@@ -1643,6 +1643,14 @@ struct cfg80211_bss *__cfg80211_get_bss(
 		if (time_after(now, bss->ts + IEEE80211_SCAN_RESULT_EXPIRE) &&
 		    !atomic_read(&bss->hold))
 			continue;
+		/*
+		 * Nor ones whose probe response data still describe the
+		 * channel before a channel switch: a new connection would
+		 * take the operating parameters of the old channel. Without
+		 * the entry, the caller scans and gets new data.
+		 */
+		if (bss->proberesp_stale && !atomic_read(&bss->hold))
+			continue;
 		if (is_bss(&bss->pub, bssid, ssid, ssid_len)) {
 			res = bss;
 			bss_ref_get(rdev, res);
@@ -1909,6 +1917,7 @@ cfg80211_update_known_bss(struct cfg8021
 		/* Override possible earlier Beacon frame IEs */
 		rcu_assign_pointer(known->pub.ies,
 				   new->pub.proberesp_ies);
+		known->proberesp_stale = new->proberesp_stale;
 		if (old) {
 			cfg80211_check_stuck_ecsa(rdev, known, old);
 			kfree_rcu((struct cfg80211_bss_ies *)old, rcu_head);
@@ -3461,6 +3470,12 @@ void cfg80211_update_assoc_bss_entry(str
 		cbss = bss_from_pub(cbss->pub.transmitted_bss);
 
 	cbss->pub.channel = chan;
+	/*
+	 * Only a probe response on the new channel replaces the probe
+	 * response data. An entry of the new channel that this one takes
+	 * over below brings its own state.
+	 */
+	cbss->proberesp_stale = !!rcu_access_pointer(cbss->pub.proberesp_ies);
 
 	list_for_each_entry(bss, &rdev->bss_list, list) {
 		if (!cfg80211_bss_type_match(bss->pub.capability,
@@ -3502,6 +3517,8 @@ void cfg80211_update_assoc_bss_entry(str
 				 nontrans_list) {
 		bss = bss_from_pub(nontrans_bss);
 		bss->pub.channel = chan;
+		bss->proberesp_stale =
+			!!rcu_access_pointer(bss->pub.proberesp_ies);
 		cfg80211_rehash_bss(rdev, bss);
 	}
 
